  "body": "What happens: on the Windows quick check of main (bacon, Intel NUC), `ui suites: lib` fails one test twice in two days: `egui_app::tests::ai_chat::basic::cancel_stops_running_worker_via_atomic_flag_and_leaves_document_unchanged` (FAIL in 58-60 s).\n\nEvidence:\n- main `d94b981` (checked 2026-11-24 ~19:30 PT, range ddee3ae..d94b981): failed.\n- main `9caa0d5` (checked 2026-11-25 ~07:00 PT, range d80dc69..9caa0d5): failed.\n- In between, bacon passed it on `c2875fc`, and lenny (desktop) passed it on nearby commits. So it is intermittent, likely a timing assumption in the cancel test on a slower machine.\n\nExpected: the test passes on every run, or it waits on an explicit signal instead of a fixed time.\n\nDone means: the cancel test waits on a deterministic condition (no fixed sleep or timeout race), and 10 repeated runs of `cargo test -p camcraft-ui --lib ai_chat::basic` pass on a Windows box.\n",
